{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U14"],
      "pins": ["U14.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U14 pin 5, named ~{RESET}, is directly connected to the GND net. In contrast, U13 pin 5 is pulled up to SERIAL_CAN_PWR_3.3V through R18.",
      "expected": "The SC16IS752 reset input is active low and should be deasserted (pulled high or driven by a controlled reset signal), not tied to ground, especially because U14 is otherwise connected to the SPI bus and to serial connectors J17/J18.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U14\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"~{RESET}\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"160\") (name \"Net-(U13-~{RESET})\") ... (node (ref \"R18\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U13\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"~{RESET}\") (pintype \"input\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(pin (num \"5\") (name \"~{RESET}\") (type \"input\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "U14 is held in reset and cannot operate. The second UART expansion controller and its serial ports (RX3/TX3/RX4/TX4) will be nonfunctional, and the SPI bus will see an unresponsive slave.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D14", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D14.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of LEDs D4, D14, and D23. No 3.3 V source, buffer output, switch, or other driver is attached to this net.",
      "expected": "A net named /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW should be a switched 3.3 V LED supply so that the connected LED anodes receive power; otherwise the LEDs cannot light.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"D4\") (value \"LED_GREEN\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"LED\") (description \"Light emitting diode\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 will remain off because their common anode supply net is floating. This removes the intended status/Ethernet/PI-activity indications associated with those LEDs.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain at least one clear anomaly: U14's active-low reset pin is tied to GND, disabling the second SC16IS752 UART controller despite its SPI and serial connections. A second likely issue is the floating /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW net, which supplies only LED anodes and has no connected 3.3 V source."
}

